.TH XCALIBER 1
.SH NAME
xcaliber \- soft-body space combat game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/xcaliber
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Xcaliber
is a port of the TempleOS game
.IR X-Caliber .
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Every ship is a breakable mass-spring truss integrated by
.IR ode (2).
The player's ship has five masses and seven springs: a nose,
two mid-body gun mounts, and two outrigger wing engines.
Springs snap when the force on them exceeds their strength,
so damage is progressive:
losing a wing loses that engine (and the missile mounted on it);
breaking a core body spring destroys the ship.
Enemy ships are a three-mass triangle and a five-mass ship with
purple pods; an enemy dies when two of its springs break
or when any of its masses overheats.
.PP
Flight is by differential thrust.
The cursor keys run the wing engines, so turning is an emergent
effect of thrusting one wing; there is no direct rotation.
Cursor-down engages the anti-spin stabilizer, which
throttles the engines against the ship's measured spin.
.PP
Weapons improve with the level:
one antimatter-ball gun on level 1, three guns on level 2,
five on level 3, and from level 4 the laser, which is held on
with the space bar, heats up (watch the temperature bar under the
control panel), and cuts out when it overheats until it cools.
The size and fuse of antimatter balls are tunable; when a ball's
fuse expires it bursts into antimatter splats that home on ships
and heat them.
Two guided wing missiles lock onto the nearest enemy in a cone
ahead of the ship (a red circle marked
.B L
or
.B R
shows the lock) and detonate on proximity or fuse.
.PP
Solar storms arrive from the left after an alarm tone:
face away from the sun or the ion shower will overheat the ship.
If a wing is bent toward the body, a spacewalker can be sent out
to straighten it; the walk takes seven and a half seconds, during
which the engines and guns are dead.
.PP
The control panel at the bottom right has a
.B SpaceWalk
button, click-to-set
.B Size
and
.B Fuse
sliders for the antimatter balls, and the laser temperature bar.
.PP
The best score and the one-time help messages persist across runs
via
.IR scorestore (2).
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "shift-up/down"
.TP
.B left / right
Run the left/right wing engine
.TP
.B up
Run both engines
.TP
.B down
Anti-spin stabilizer
.TP
.B space
Fire guns; from level 4, hold for the laser
.TP
.B ctrl-left / z
Launch the left missile
.TP
.B ctrl-right / x
Launch the right missile
.TP
.B shift-up/down
Larger/smaller shot; also
.B p
and
.B o
.TP
.B shift-right/left
Longer/shorter fuse; also
.B ]
and
.B [
.TP
.B w
Spacewalk (when a wing is bent)
.TP
.B + / -
Change level
.TP
.B Enter
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TF /icons/temple/xcaliber_*.bit
.TP
.B /icons/temple/xcaliber_*.bit
sprites from the original's DolDoc bins
.TP
.B /fonts/temple/temple.font
the 8x8 system font used for all text
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/xcaliber.b
