.SH BUGS
The laser is two things that do not agree, and both are the
original's.
What it damages is chosen geometrically, in the derivative: the
nearest mass whose perpendicular offset from the beam is inside
its own radius.
What is drawn is a pixel walk \- the beam is laid down a pixel at
a time and stops at the first that is neither black nor white \-
so a shot in flight, an explosion ring or an enemy's drawn body
will end it short of what it is actually burning, and white text
will not.
The original's noise and sweep sound effects are approximated
with stepped tones on a single voice.
The shift and ctrl cursor chords work only where the platform
delivers shifter key events; the plain-key equivalents above
always work.
There is no pull-down menu tree.
